Instruction for postprocess.ex (embedded version)*

*Note that there is a self-standing version of postprocessing binaries 
in /NEMO3D/postprocess/bin directory. 

postprocess.ex [options]: postprocess outputs of NEMO3D.
   Task 1. project electron/hole wavefunctions into bulk-band Bloch functions.
   Task 2. calculate dipole moments of electron-hole pair. (two options available see below)
   Task 3. calculate angular momenta of electron/hole wave functions.
   Task 4. calculate electron-nuclear hyperfine interaction 
           and dephasing/decoherence times due to the interaction.  
   Task 5. calculate time-reversal states (Kramers' degenerate state). 
   Task 6. calculate Coulomb/exchange interactions of electron-hole pair. 
          (Not quite implemented yet for this embedded postprocess.ex. 
           Please use the self-standing PostProcess.ex for this task.)
   Task 7. more to come .......
   * You can turn on/off these tasks with [options]. (see below)

How to create postprocess.ex:
   cd /NEMO3D/build
   edit file "make.inc" to have POSTPROCESS = Embedded
   make nemo3d   
     (nemo3d.ex will be created in nemo3d/bin directory)
   ln -s nemo3d.ex postprocess.ex
     (shoft-link nemo3d.ex to postprocess.ex) 

Required files to run postprocess.ex: 
   1.NEMO3D input/output files)
        filename.xml (NEMO3D input file)
        filename.nd_aType (atom type; not needed for Task 5) 
        filename.nd_nbrIndx (nearest neighbor index; not needed for Task5)
        filename.nd_rAtom (atom position; not needed for Task 5)
        filename.nd_evec_# (electron or/and hole wavefunction)
   2.Table fiels for postprocessing:
        coulomb.table (table needed only for coulomb/exchange calculation)      
        dipole.table  (table needed only for dipole moment calculation)
        These files are located in the current directory.

Options to run postprocess.ex
   --data filename: specify the filesnames of NEMO3D input/output files
                         (filename.xml, filename.nd_rAtom, etc)
   --electron N n1 n2 ....:
          N is the number of electron wavefunctions to include in calculations.
          n1, n2, ... are the indices of electron wavefunctions to read
          from filename.nd_evec_n1, filename.nd_evec_n2, ....
          There should be N number of electron wavefunctions.
   --hole N n1 n2 ....:
          N is the number of hole wavefunctions to include in calculations.
          n1, n2, ... are the indices of hole wavefunctions to read
          from filename.nd_evec_n1, filename.nd_evec_n2, ....
          There should be N number of hole wavefunctions.
   --dipole:
          calculate dipole moments/Oscillator strengths of electron-hole pairs.
          include both intra-orbital and inter-orbital dipole moments.
   --dipole_approximation:
          calculate dipole moments <X>, <Y>, <Z> including only intra-orbital dipole moments.
   --projection:
          project electron/hole wavefunctions onto bulk-band Bloch functions.
   --time_reversal --evec_file filename:
          calculate time-reversal states of a wave function given by filename.
          The file should be a NEMO3D outputfile with suffix ".nd_evec_#"
   --decoherence:
	  calculate electron-nuclear hyperfine interaction, nuclear magnetic filed, 
          and electron dephasing/decoherence time.
   --angularmomentum:
	  calculate the angular momentum of electron/hole wave functions.

Example 1:
   postprocess.ex --data QuantumDot --electron 2 6 7 --hole 3 1 2 3 \
                  --dipole --projection
   What this will do:
   1. QuantumDot.xml, QuantumDot.nd_aType, QuantumDot.nd_nbrIndx, 
      and QuantumDot.nd_rAtom be read.
   2. Two electron wavefunctions will be given by QuantumDot.nd_evec_6 
      and QuantumDot.nd_evec_7.
   3. Three hole wavefunctions will be given by QuantumDot.nd_evec_1, 
      QuantumDot.nd_evec_2, and QuantumDot.nd_evec_3
   4. The dipole moments between the two electron and the three hole 
      wavefunctions will be calculated.
   5. The two electron wavefunctions and the three hole wavefunctions
      will be projected onto bulk-band Bloch functions.

Example 2:
   postprocess.ex --data QuantumWire --time_reversal --evec_file QuantumWire.nd_evec_5
   What this will do:
   1. QuantumWire.xml and QuantumWire.nd_evec_5 will be read. 
   2. Note that other files (__.nd_aType, __.nd_rAtom, __.nd_nbrIndx)
      are not needed for this "time_reversal" task.
   3. The time-reversal state of the wave function given by "QuantumWire.nd_evec_5"
      will be created, and written in new file "QuantumWire.nd_evec_5_tr"

Example 3:
   postprocess.ex --data QuantumWell --angularmomentum --electron 2 1 2 
   What this will do:
   1. QuantumWell.xml, QuantumWell.nd_aType, QuantumWell.nd_rAtom,
      QuantumWell.nd_nbrIndx, QuantumWell.nd_evec_1, and QuantumWell.nd_evec_2 
      will be read.
   2. The angular momentum of the two electron wave functions given by 
      QuantumWell.nd_evec_1 and QuantumWell.nd_evec_2 will be calculated.

Exampe 4:
   postprocess.ex --data QDWL --dipole_approximation --electron 1 1 --hole 1 2
   What this will do:
   1. QDWL.xml, QDWL.nd_aType, QDWL.nd_rAtom,
      QDWL.nd_nbrIndx, QDWL.nd_evec_1, and QDWL.nd_evec_2 will be read.
      All the listed files should be available in the working directory. 
   2. The dipole moment of the two wave functions given by
      QDWL.nd_evec_1 and QDWL.nd_evec_2 will be calculated.
      i.e. <n1|X|n2>, <n1|Y|n2>, <n1|Z|n2> 
      Note that the dipole moments are complex numbers. 
   3. In contrast to the option "--dipole", this option "--dipole_approximation"
      does not include inter-orbital dipole moments. It only includes intra-orbital 
      dipole moments. Therefore, file "dipole.table" is not needed in this option.                   
   4. Although the two wave functions are labeled as electron or hole, 
      they do not have to be electron or hole wave functions. 
      You can get dipole moments between two electron wave functions 
      by listing one wave function as an electron, and the other as a hole. 





 
